#: hivepress-vendor-analytics.php:706
msgid "On the first of each month, vendors can be sent a summary of the month just gone, with a button that opens their full report. Switching it on sends to every vendor; the second setting hands each vendor the choice for themselves. Edit the wording under HivePress > Emails."
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-vendor-analytics.php:711
msgid "Monthly reports"
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-vendor-analytics.php:712
msgid "Email vendors a monthly summary of their analytics"
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-vendor-analytics.php:713
msgid "While this is off nothing is sent and nothing is shown to vendors. Switching it on means every vendor is emailed on the first of the month, unless they have turned it off for themselves."
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-vendor-analytics.php:720
msgid "Vendor choice"
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-vendor-analytics.php:721
msgid "Let vendors decide whether to receive them"
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-vendor-analytics.php:722
msgid "Adds the choice to each vendor's own settings page, so they can turn the email off. Switch this off to keep the decision yourself: vendors then see nothing about it and everyone is emailed. Any choices vendors have already made are remembered and come back if you switch this on again."
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-vendor-analytics.php:729
#: hivepress-vendor-analytics.php:4664
msgid "Quiet months"
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-vendor-analytics.php:730
msgid "Include vendors with no activity to report"
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-vendor-analytics.php:731
msgid "A month with no views, messages, bookings or earnings produces a page of zeros, so this is off by default. While vendors can decide for themselves, each one can override this on their own settings page."
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-vendor-analytics.php:740
msgid "Data"
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-vendor-analytics.php:741
msgid "Figures are stored as daily totals in two small database tables on your own site."
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-vendor-analytics.php:746
msgid "Retention (days)"
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-vendor-analytics.php:747
msgid "Daily aggregates older than this are deleted by a daily cron job. Set to 0 to keep data forever."
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-vendor-analytics.php:758
msgid "Removing the plugin"
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-vendor-analytics.php:759
msgid "What happens if you ever delete this plugin. WordPress always shows a \"will also delete its data\" warning on the delete screen, but unless the box below is ticked your analytics and settings are kept, so you can reinstall later and carry on where you left off. Deactivating never removes anything."
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-vendor-analytics.php:764
msgid "Delete all data"
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-vendor-analytics.php:765
msgid "Permanently delete all analytics data when this plugin is deleted"
msgstr ""

#: hivepress-vendor-analytics.php:766
msgid "Removes the two analytics tables, every setting on this tab and the internal order and booking markers. This cannot be undone."
msgstr ""

